<h2>One dental home for your household</h2>
<p>Family dentistry means caring for the same patients through the stages of adult life — from a teenager's permanent teeth to comprehensive preventive and restorative care for adults. Coordinating that care under one roof saves you time, money, and the headache of bouncing between offices.</p>
<p>We see teens and adults. <!-- CONFIRM: minimum patient age (old site said "ages 12+"). --></p>

<h2>What's included</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li>Comprehensive exams and digital X-rays</li>
  <li>Cleanings (prophylaxis) and periodontal maintenance</li>
  <li>Fluoride treatments and dental sealants where they help</li>
  <li>Tooth-colored fillings</li>
  <li>Guidance for grinding, clenching, and bite concerns</li>
  <li>Mouthguards for sports and night-time grinding</li>
</ul>

<h2>What a typical visit looks like</h2>
<p>Most healthy patients are on a six-month recall — a routine exam, a professional cleaning, and X-rays once a year. Patients with a history of gum disease or more complex needs may be on a three- or four-month interval. We always tell you why, never just "because."</p>

<h2>New to the practice?</h2>
<p>Visit our <a href="/new-patients/">new patients page</a> to learn what to expect and download any paperwork ahead of your first visit. We try to make first appointments as smooth as possible.</p>

<h2>Care for every stage of adult life</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><strong>Teens:</strong> checkups, sealants, sports mouthguards and <a href="/services/wisdom-teeth-removal/">wisdom teeth</a> evaluations before they cause trouble</li>
  <li><strong>Adults:</strong> cleanings, <a href="/services/dental-fillings/">fillings</a>, <a href="/services/crowns-bridges/">crowns</a>, <a href="/services/teeth-whitening/">whitening</a> and <a href="/services/tmj-night-guards/">night guards</a> for grinding</li>
  <li><strong>Older adults:</strong> <a href="/services/gum-disease-treatment/">gum health</a>, replacing missing teeth with <a href="/services/dental-implants/">implants</a> or <a href="/services/dentures/">dentures</a>, and keeping existing dental work in good shape</li>
</ul>
<p>Because Dr. Phillips also places implants and does extractions in-house, your family doesn't get referred out for most treatment. You keep the same dentist, the same records and the same team.</p>

<h2>Why families in Tempe choose us</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li>A private, single-doctor practice: you see Dr. Matthew Phillips at every visit</li>
  <li>Clear explanations, with your X-rays shown to you, and no pressure</li>
  <li>Written estimates before treatment, so there are no surprise bills</li>
  <li>Convenient for families across Tempe, Mesa, Chandler, Gilbert and Ahwatukee</li>
</ul>

<h2>Insurance and costs</h2>
<p>We accept most major PPO plans. Most plans cover preventive visits at or near 100%, so routine checkups often cost little or nothing out of pocket. No insurance? Start with our <a href="/special-offers/">$49 new-patient exam and X-rays</a>, and see <a href="/insurance-financing/">insurance and financing</a> for payment options.</p>

